google-service-account.json
# Firebase CLIENT config for FCM push. This one IS committed, deliberately.
# It is not a secret - it ships inside every APK, and its API key is restricted
# to this package name plus the signing certificate. More importantly, EAS builds
# from what git tracks, so ignoring it produces a build with no Firebase config
# at all: the app installs, looks fine, silently never obtains a push token, and
# every push is delivered to nobody. That is the failure this rule caused.
# The SECRET half is the FCM service account key, which is uploaded to expo.dev
# and never lives in this repo (see google-service-account.json above for the
# separate Google Play key).
!google-services.json
